Reason:
The fix involves explicitly invalidating the SLEEP and WAKE TCSes before flushing new data. This is achieved by calling `rpmh_rsc_invalidate()` to clear any stale data. Additionally, the `rpmh_invalidate()` function is simplified to handle the invalidation of the batch cache directly, ensuring that the cache is cleared and marked as dirty before any new data is processed, thus preventing the old data from interfering with the new flush operation.

